# Line endings are decided here, not by whatever git happens to be installed.
#
# core.autocrlf lives in Git for Windows' own system config
# (C:/Program Files/Git/etc/gitconfig) and does NOT travel with a clone, so the
# same tree that is clean on this machine reported ~385 modified files when it
# was opened from a Linux VM: CRLF on disk, LF in the repository, and nothing
# telling git the two are the same file. This does tell it.
#
# Measured 2026-09-04 before adding this: every blob already stores LF and
# every working-tree file is already CRLF, so these rules describe what is
# there rather than changing it.
* text=auto

# Windows batch scripts: cmd.exe can misread a .bat that arrives with LF, so
# these are checked out CRLF on every platform. Still stored as LF.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Never converted, never diffed as text. Git detects most of these on its own;
# saying so leaves nothing to detection.
*.woff2       binary
*.woff        binary
*.otf         binary
*.ttf         binary
*.png         binary
*.ico         binary
*.bin         binary
*.gz          binary
*.traineddata binary
*.dll         binary
*.exe         binary
*.db          binary
*.db-shm      binary
*.db-wal      binary
